QuestGuidance.Register("en",410,{
[13089]="70050B1B\n1\tComplete each of the major story-lines for the Dwarf-holds\tHelp out in all major affairs in the Dwarf-holds.\n2\tComplete 'Into the Ironfold'\030Assist Náin with Hammerstead and Utterby\030Follow Nori's trail\030Assist with affairs in Thornholt\030Assist in the Steel Keep\030Assist in the Glimmerdeep mines\030Assist at Stormwall\tHelp out in all major affairs in the Dwarf-holds, including: 'Into the Ironfold', 'An Audience with the Boy King', 'An Unexpected Story', 'Scars of Battle', 'Across the Chasm', 'In the Halls of Thikil-gundu', and 'Etterfang.'\n3\tTalk to Stráhek the Stout\tStráhek can be found in Skarháld in the Grey Mountains. You should talk with Stráhek the Stout about the Zhélruka efforts to establish themselves in the Grey Mountains.\n",
[13090]="7006A9E9\n1\tTalk to Belondor\tNashôn has asked you to report to Belondor in Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall in Umbar Baharbêl with news of the guards' progress in the sewers beneath the Sail-haven.\n",
[13091]="700379C0\n1\tDefeat the siege trolls assaulting Helm's monument ([see journal]/5)\tHelm Hammerhand's statue must be defended from the enemies seeking to desecrate his memorial and dishearten the soldiers guarding the dike. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[13092]="7003A4A8\n1\tDefeat waves of enemies attacking Helm's Statue or weapon caches ([see journal]/7)\tHelm Hammerhand's statue must be defended from the enemies seeking to desecrate his memorial and dishearten the soldiers guarding the dike. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[13093]="7002F841\n1\tDefeat marsh-flies in the Stinging Bog (total: 10)\tThe Stinging Bog is on the far side of the road from Feldburg. You should kill marsh-flies in the Stinging Bog.\n2\tReturn to Captain Agelmund\tCaptain Agelmund awaits you at Feldburg. You should return to Captain Agelmund now that you have done as he asked of you.\n",
[13094]="70066CDF\n1\tPick up the honey pot\tLeithiel has asked you to distract a swarm of bees with some honey. You should pick up the jar of honey. The honey is next to Leithiel at Bergraw in Pinnath Gelin.\n2\tPlace the honeypot\030Collect yeast\tYou should place the honeypot a ways away from the barrel of grapes. A good spot for the honeypot can be found at Bergraw in Pinnath Gelin.\n3\tBring the yeast to Leithiel\tYou should bring the yeast you've collected to Leithiel at her vineyard in Pinnath Gelin.\n",
[13095]="7001752E\n1\tBring the fragments to Gelirwen at the Shadowed Refuge\030Collect the queen's fragment (quantity: see journal)\tGelirwen is at the Shadowed Refuge. You discovered an item on the master of Skûmfil. It is possible that another half of the item rests on the other combatant at the location.\n",
[13096]="700176B5\n1\tBring the fragments to Gelirwen at the Shadowed Refuge\030Collect the king's fragment (quantity: see journal)\tGelirwen is at the Shadowed Refuge. You discovered an item on the grodbog-queen in Skûmfil. It is possible that another half of the item rests on the other combatant at the location.\n",
[13097]="7007021F\n1\tFind the Narghâk workshop in Starkhaven, on the western shore of the Fearwater\tCorudan wants to search for the Narghâk workshop he believes to be located somewhere among the buildings on the western shore of the Fearwater, in Starkhaven.\n2\tExamine one of the unusual-looking weapons at the Narghâk workshop\tYou should examine one of the unusual-looking weapons at the Narghâk workshop on the western shore of the Fearwater, in Starkhaven.\n3\tPlans nearby may describe the construction process for designing such Narghâk weapons as those located at the Starkhaven workshop. You should examine the plans and defeat any who try to stop you.\t\n4\tExamine the marked barrel by the Narghâk workshop\tWhat did the engineer think to retrieve from the marked barrel by the Narghâk workshop?\n5\tExamine another marked barrel by the Narghâk workshop\tWhat did the engineer think to retrieve from the marked barrel by the Narghâk workshop?\n6\tTalk to Corudan at the Narghâk workshop in Starkhaven\tCorudan has come to the Narghâk workshop at Starkhaven.\n7\tDeprive Corsairs in Sûg Nidar of Narghâk bottles (total: 6)\tCorudan has learned that Heirsworn Corsairs throughout Sûg Nidar may carry small glass bottles containing quantities of Narghâk.\n8\tBring the bottles of Narghâk to Corudan at the workshop in Starkhaven\tCorudan waits for word of your success at the Narghâk workshop on the western shore of the Fearwater, in Starkhaven.\n",
[13098]="70052943\n1\tSeek out the Ungoledan encampment in Laerlad\tCôs Braen can be found in the southern edge of Laerlad. You should seek out the Ungoledan encampment of Côs Braen in Laerlad.\n2\tDefeat Ungoledain at Côs Braen (total: 10)\030Defeat spiders at Côs Braen (total: 6)\030Destroy vile spider totems (total: 8)\tCôs Braen can be found in the southern edge of Laerlad. You should defeat those you find in Côs Braen.\n3\tTalk to Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Blómgard. You should talk to Radagast.\n4\tTalk to Odahild\tOdahild can be found in Blómgard. You should talk to Odahild.\n5\tTalk to Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Blómgard. You should talk to Radagast.\n",
[13099]="70058CEE\n1\tCollect stolen dwarf-relics in Tûr Ágal (total: 10)\tChests of stolen dwarf-relics can be found in Tûr Ágal. You have discovered chests filled with stolen dwarf-relics in Tûr Ágal. You should collect them and see that they are returned to the Gabil'akkâ.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have collected many chests of stolen dwarf-relics in Tûr Ágal.\n",
[13100]="70008281\n1\tCollect the broken ornament\tGurmagath can be found on a hillock in the north-eastern area of Taur Gonwaith, south-east of Lin Giliath. Thaliollang has asked you, in memory of Lachenn, to hunt down the chieftain of the Stone-trolls, Gurmagath, and retrieve Lachenn's ornament so that it can be restored to a place of honour.\n2\tTalk to Thaliollang\030Collect Broken Ornament\tThaliollang is at Lin Giliath, north-west of Taur Gonwaith. Thaliollang is waiting for you to return with the ornament you retrieved from Gurmagath.\n",
[13101]="70001137\n1\tSearch Ost Dúrgonn for the stolen stones\tCave-claws infest the ruins of Ost Dúrgonn, north of the road and Barachen's camp. Heithur Ironfist believes that the cave-claws of Ost Dúrgonn might have carried away the stones that his company was bringing to Glóin and perhaps swarmed in such strength as to defeat the dwarves.\n2\tTalk to Tóki Whitebeard\tHeithur Ironfist is at Barachen's camp, east of the Last Bridge and south of the road, on a sloping hill in the shadow of tall cliffs. You have learned from Tóki Whitebeard that the stones his company was transporting have been stolen by trolls, apparently aided by the monstrous cave-claw you defeated.\n",
[13102]="7005857C\n1\tDraw out and defeat Akhún\tDûn Traikh lies west of Drenghól. Einar suggested meddling with the Angmarim weapon stores to draw Akhún out so that you can reclaim his sword.\n2\tDeliver the sword to Einar\tYou have reclaimed Einar's sword. You should return it to its rightful owner at Drenghól.\n",
[13103]="70020B47\n1\tGet the shrew-stomping boots from the nearby crate\tThe boots needed for stomping on shrews can be found near the stairs of the Festival Garden. You should collect the boots from the crate and drag them to your skill bar, for they will be needed to deter shrews.\n2\tYou have been given boots for stomping on shrews; you should slot these as a skill and enter the garden\tThe pesky shrews can be found in the centre of the garden in Duillond's Festival Garden space, and the shrew-stomping boots are in your inventory. You should locate the boots in your inventory and slot them as a skill. These boots can be used to stomp on obnoxious shrews infesting the garden. When you have done so, you should wait for the shrew-whacking game to begin in the garden's centre. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Boots of Quite-imaginable Power' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres.\n3\tSlot the shrew-stomping boots in your skill bar and wait for the onslaught\tThe pesky shrews can be found in the centre space of Duillond's Festival Garden. Logethuil has asked you to defeat many shrews, and also to ensure the protection of the tender young plants attempting to grow in this hostile environment. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Boots of Quite-imaginable Power' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres.\n4\tDrive away pesky shrews (total: 10)\030Plant seedlings in mounds of soil (total: 5)\tThe pesky shrews can be found in the centre space of Duillond's Festival Garden. Logethuil has asked you to defeat many shrews, and also plant seedlings so that the garden may thrive. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Boots of Quite-imaginable Power' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tTalk to Logethuil\tLogethuil is in the Garden of Duillond. You should bring news of your success to Logethuil.\n",
[13104]="70058355\n1\tDestroy the stone-claw nests within Klórgren\tThe burrows of Klórgren can be found on the eastern edges of Elderslade. You should destroy the stone-claw nests within Klórgren.\n2\tDestroy the stone-claw nests within Klórgren (total: 10)\tThe burrows of Klórgren can be found on the eastern edges of Elderslade. You should destroy the stone-claw nests within Klórgren.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many stone-claw nests within Klórgren.\n",
[13105]="7002C6A7\n1\tTalk to Lanbert at the base of the Cuthstan in the Wailing Hills\tLanbert is in charge of the Rohirrim camp at the Cuthstan in Wailing Hills. Gadda has asked you to seek out Lanbert at the Cuthstan.\n",
[13106]="7005A686\n1\tDefeat stone-smashers in Gundabad (total: 8)\030Search for signs of stone-smashers\tStone-smashers found throughout Gundabad. You should defeat stone-smashers for Bráthi. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeat many stone-smashers in Gundabad.\n",
[13107]="700006AB\n1\tTalk to Aric the Stone-speaker\tFind Aric by travelling south across the Great East Road and beyond Talath Gaun. Venture into Harloeg, as far south into the swamp as you can journey into the ruins there. Frideric has sent you to speak with Aric, the Stone-speaker.\n",
[13108]="700017AE\n1\tFind and defeat the Stonehold Chief\tThe Stonehold Chief is in the goblin camp on the southern hills of Annúndir, east of Amon Raith. You should find and defeat the Stonehold Chief.\n2\tDefeat the Stonehold Chief\tThe Stonehold Chief is in the goblin camp on the southern hills of Annúndir, east of Amon Raith. You should defeat the Stonehold Chief.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the Stonehold Chief, eliminating the greatest weight of the goblin threat in Annúndir.\n",
[13109]="7004DCE4\n1\tCollect crude stones from the slopes of Erebor (total: 12)\tCrude stones can be found along the western slopes of Erebor. Ambassador Spakorth has asked you to gather crude stones from the slopes of Erebor that they might be carved into rune-stones by the Stout-axes.\n2\tStout-axe rune-carvers can be found in Erebor. You have gathered many stones from the slopes of Erebor and should now deliver them to the Stout-axe rune-carvers in Erebor.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have delivered many crude stones to the Stout-axe rune-carvers.\n",
[13110]="70064F6E\n1\tGurkrak keeps watch on Gwathrenost and brutally dispatches those foolish or daring enough to enter the Witch-king's citadel unbidden. You must defeat Gurkrak and enter Gwathrenost.\t\n2\tAscend Gwathrenost and enter the Castellan's chambers\tThe Castellan's chambers can be found atop a set of winding stairs within Gwathrenost. You must find the Castellan's chambers and defeat Castellan Obáshurz if you are to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.\n3\tDefeat Castellan Obáshurz\tOne of the last remnants of the reign of the Steward of Angmar, Castellan Obáshurz tends Gwathrenost and dutifully serves his masters: High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd. You must defeat Castellan Obáshurz.\n4\tAscend Gwathrenost and enter Tham Mornarcham\tTham Mornarcham can be found atop Gwathrenost. You must ascend Gwathrenost and reach Tham Mornarcham to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.\n5\tDefeat High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd\tHigh Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd await in Tham Mornarcham, the Seat of the the Witch-king. High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd must be defeated before they can wield the shard of Tauressar to subjugate the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.\n6\tDestroy the Shard of Tauressar\tSevered from the Vandassar of Rhudaur, the shard of Tauressar is possessed of a terrible enchantment capable of swaying the hearts and minds of those who swear oaths upon it—willingly or not. You must destroy the shard of Tauressar.\n7\tCompleted: Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel (Tier 1)\tWith the destruction of the shard of Tauressar and the final downfall of the Iron Crown, a new day dawns in Angmar. You have completed 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel' on Tier 1. NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Gwathrenost, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Monday, Thursday, and Saturday.\n",
[13111]="70064F70\n1\tGurkrak keeps watch on Gwathrenost and brutally dispatches those foolish or daring enough to enter the Witch-king's citadel unbidden. You must defeat Gurkrak and enter Gwathrenost.\t\n2\tAscend Gwathrenost and enter the Castellan's chambers\tThe Castellan's chambers can be found atop a set of winding stairs within Gwathrenost. You must find the Castellan's chambers and defeat Castellan Obáshurz if you are to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.\n3\tDefeat Castellan Obáshurz\tOne of the last remnants of the reign of the Steward of Angmar, Castellan Obáshurz tends Gwathrenost and dutifully serves his masters: High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd. You must defeat Castellan Obáshurz.\n4\tAscend Gwathrenost and enter Tham Mornarcham\tTham Mornarcham can be found atop Gwathrenost. You must ascend Gwathrenost and reach Tham Mornarcham to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.\n5\tDefeat High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd\tHigh Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd await in Tham Mornarcham, the Seat of the the Witch-king. High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd must be defeated before they can wield the shard of Tauressar to subjugate the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.\n6\tDestroy the Shard of Tauressar\tSevered from the Vandassar of Rhudaur, the shard of Tauressar is possessed of a terrible enchantment capable of swaying the hearts and minds of those who swear oaths upon it—willingly or not. You must destroy the shard of Tauressar.\n7\tCompleted: Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel (Tier 2)\tWith the destruction of the shard of Tauressar and the final downfall of the Iron Crown, a new day dawns in Angmar. You have completed 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel' on Tier 2. NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Gwathrenost, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Thursday.\n",
[13112]="70064F6F\n1\tGurkrak keeps watch on Gwathrenost and brutally dispatches those foolish or daring enough to enter the Witch-king's citadel unbidden. You must defeat Gurkrak and enter Gwathrenost.\t\n2\tAscend Gwathrenost and enter the Castellan's chambers\tThe Castellan's chambers can be found atop a set of winding stairs within Gwathrenost. You must find the Castellan's chambers and defeat Castellan Obáshurz if you are to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.\n3\tDefeat Castellan Obáshurz\tOne of the last remnants of the reign of the Steward of Angmar, Castellan Obáshurz tends Gwathrenost and dutifully serves his masters: High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd. You must defeat Castellan Obáshurz.\n4\tAscend Gwathrenost and enter Tham Mornarcham\tTham Mornarcham can be found atop Gwathrenost. You must ascend Gwathrenost and reach Tham Mornarcham to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.\n5\tDefeat High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd\tHigh Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd await in Tham Mornarcham, the Seat of the the Witch-king. High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd must be defeated before they can wield the shard of Tauressar to subjugate the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.\n6\tDestroy the Shard of Tauressar\tSevered from the Vandassar of Rhudaur, the shard of Tauressar is possessed of a terrible enchantment capable of swaying the hearts and minds of those who swear oaths upon it—willingly or not. You must destroy the shard of Tauressar.\n7\tCompleted: Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel (Tier 3)\tWith the destruction of the shard of Tauressar and the final downfall of the Iron Crown, a new day dawns in Angmar. You have completed 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel' on Tier 3. NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Gwathrenost, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Thursday.\n",
