[13114]="70064F71\n1\tGurkrak keeps watch on Gwathrenost and brutally dispatches those foolish or daring enough to enter the Witch-king's citadel unbidden. You must defeat Gurkrak and enter Gwathrenost.\t\n2\tAscend Gwathrenost and enter the Castellan's chambers\tThe Castellan's chambers can be found atop a set of winding stairs within Gwathrenost. You must find the Castellan's chambers and defeat Castellan Obáshurz if you are to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.\n3\tDefeat Castellan Obáshurz\tOne of the last remnants of the reign of the Steward of Angmar, Castellan Obáshurz tends Gwathrenost and dutifully serves his masters: High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd. You must defeat Castellan Obáshurz.\n4\tAscend Gwathrenost and enter Tham Mornarcham\tTham Mornarcham can be found atop Gwathrenost. You must ascend Gwathrenost and reach Tham Mornarcham to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.\n5\tDefeat High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd\tHigh Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd await in Tham Mornarcham, the Seat of the the Witch-king. High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd must be defeated before they can wield the shard of Tauressar to subjugate the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.\n6\tDestroy the Shard of Tauressar\tSevered from the Vandassar of Rhudaur, the shard of Tauressar is possessed of a terrible enchantment capable of swaying the hearts and minds of those who swear oaths upon it—willingly or not. You must destroy the shard of Tauressar.\n7\tCompleted: Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel (Tier 5)\tWith the destruction of the shard of Tauressar and the final downfall of the Iron Crown, a new day dawns in Angmar. You have completed 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel' on Tier 5. NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Gwathrenost, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Thursday.\n",
[13115]="7002CA93\n1\tTalk to Sabert, your one remaining friend at Stangard\tSabert, your friend at Stangard, still guards the gate. You should speak with Sabert upon your return to Stangard.\n2\tAsk Byrnstan about the death of Stanric\030Ask Uthrad about the death of Stanric\030Ask Wada about the death of Stanric\030Ask Athulf about the death of Stanric\030Ask Adalbert about the death of Stanric\tMen of Stangard can be found throughout the town. You should question many men about the death of Stanric, for Gadda suspects treachery on Sithric's part.\n3\tReturn to Sabert at the front gate\tSabert guards the front gate of Stangard. You should speak with Sabert at once about all that transpired during your questioning.\n",
[13116]="70034B93\n1\tListen to Iothete's tale\tIothete is in his hut in the woods in the Whitshaws. You should speak with Iothete and hear his tale.\n2\tTalk to Iothete\tIothete is in his hut in the woods in the Whitshaws. You should speak with Iothete.\n",
[13117]="70045219\n1\tGather trampled grass (total: 8)\030Gather sticks (total: 6)\tLady Glánhar has asked you to go out of Ost Rimmon and gather sticks and trampled grass for her straw-man project.\n2\tReturn to Glánhar\tYou should return to Lady Glánhar in Ost Rimmon with the sticks and trampled grass you gathered for her straw-man project.\n3\tTalk to Narvellon\tAsk Narvellon the Beacon-keeper in Ost Rimmon for weapons, helms, and rough cloth for Lady Glánhar's straw men.\n4\tCollect helms (total: 6)\030Collect swords (total: 6)\030Gather cloth (total: 6)\tHelms and swords can be found throughout Ost Rimmon. Rough cloth can be found in Ost Rimmon's store-house. Gather helms, swords, and rough cloth for Lady Glánhar's straw men.\n5\tReturn to Lady Glánhar\tYou should bring the helms, swords, and cloth for the straw-men to Glánhar in the centre of Ost Rimmon.\n6\tBring the materials to Bargwen\tBargwen is south-west of Lady Glánhar in Ost Rimmon. Bring the materials for Lady Glánhar's straw men to Bargwen for assembly.\n7\tReturn to Lady Glánhar\tYou should tell Lady Glánhar that Bargwen has begun work on her straw men-at-arms.\n",
[13118]="7006A167\n1\tPursue Khâshap!\tKhâshap has lured you into the Gut, and has turned the streets against you. Give chase as he makes his way to his master!\n2\tChase Khâshap to the Gate of Sorrow!\tKhâshap has fled deeper into the back streets. Continue your pursuit before he delivers the Bile of Ifrinn!\n3\tDefeat Utho the Grasper\tKhâshap has left you to deal with his most trusted cohort, Utho the Grasper. Defeat Utho the Grasper.\n4\tFollow Khâshap to the Gate of Storms\tKhâshap has taken to the Fleetfast. He is running out of places to run. You must corner him at last!\n5\tDefeat Khâshap, Irinn's Abomination\tKhâshap has been cornered at the Gate of Storms. You must defeat him before he can make his final attempt at delivering this Bile of Ifrinn to his master.\n",
[13119]="7006A165\n1\tPursue Khâshap!\tKhâshap has lured you into the Gut, and has turned the streets against you. Give chase as he makes his way to his master!\n2\tChase Khâshap to the Gate of Sorrow!\tKhâshap has fled deeper into the back streets. Continue your pursuit before he delivers the Bile of Ifrinn!\n3\tDefeat Utho the Grasper\tKhâshap has left you to deal with his most trusted cohort, Utho the Grasper. Defeat Utho the Grasper.\n4\tFollow Khâshap to the Gate of Storms\tKhâshap has taken to the Fleetfast. He is running out of places to run. You must corner him at last!\n5\tDefeat Khâshap, Irinn's Abomination\tKhâshap has been cornered at the Gate of Storms. You must defeat him before he can make his final attempt at delivering this Bile of Ifrinn to his master.\n",
